### F-MENUS-01
- symptom: On the galaxy map (the player's M/N map), Tab never moves keyboard focus — every Tab press toggles a random chart lens instead, so keyboard-only players cannot reach the layer buttons, plot/engage rail controls or any other focusable control on the screen (arrows only serve the search list); focus is effectively owned away from the dialog.
- severity: major
- route: open map (M/N) → press Tab (or Shift+Tab) with focus anywhere in the screen
- owner: src/ui/galaxyMap.js:5327-5347 (`galaxyMapScreen.onKey`, Tab branch)
- evidence: `if (key === 'tab') { event.preventDefault(); … this._layers[this._currentLayerFocus] = !this._layers[this._currentLayerFocus]; … }` — the branch unconditionally preventDefaults Tab with no text-entry/shift distinction and no comment, and no other traversal exists for the screen's DOM controls. `src/ui/input.js:348-389` routes every modal keydown to `def.onKey` before anything else, and `src/ui/screenManager.js:143-159` (`_trapKeydown`) only intervenes at the focus edges, so in-screen Tab is wholly consumed here. No help entry, theme doc or check records "Tab cycles lenses" as intent.
- suggested_fix: delete the Tab branch so native traversal plus the ScreenManager trap own Tab (mirroring every other modal screen); move lens toggling, if wanted, to the screen's context menu (`galaxyMap.js:7729` already lists lens verbs there) or an unclaimed key.
- confidence: high

### F-MENUS-02
- symptom: On the legacy star chart, the drawn per-sector price tag next to a node can never render — the player trades at stations and learns prices, but the chart never shows one regardless of how many markets were visited.
- severity: minor (legacy surface: `src/ui/input.js:503` keeps starmap for tools/checks only; M/N open galaxyMap via `src/ui/input.js:504-513` and `src/ui/uiRoot.js:1342-1358`)
- route: star chart (legacy) → visit a market → open chart → no buy/sell pair beside the sector node
- owner: src/ui/screens/starmap.js:1280-1289 (`_drawNodes`)
- evidence: `starmap.js:1280-1282` reads `state.player.marketMemory[s.id]` where `s` is a sector node (`_draw()` builds nodes from sectors, `starmap.js:1122-1123`), but the single writer keys the memory by station id: `src/systems/economy.js:2514-2515` `const memory = ensurePlayerMarketMemory(…); const stationMemory = memory[stationId] || …`. The sector-keyed lookup is always `undefined`, so `commQuote` is never truthy and the block is dead code; the sidebar (`starmap.js:1401` → `_marketMemoryHtml` → `marketMemoryStationOverlays`, which maps stations→sectors) is correct while the canvas label is not.
- suggested_fix: derive the node label from `marketMemoryStationOverlays(state, this._commodityId)` filtered to `o.sectorId === s.id` (best overlay), or remove the dead canvas block in favor of the working sidebar section.
- confidence: high

### F-MENUS-03
- symptom: In Shipworks, clicking a hardpoint node on the hull dial can be silently swallowed: the node lights up (selection state set) but no chooser opens, no deny cue, no receipt — a control that does nothing.
- severity: minor
- route: docked berth → Shipworks → click a dial node during the window after a re-render dropped the slot nodes (rebuilt on the next projection frame)
- owner: src/ui/station/screens/shipworks.js:3037-3041 (jig `onPick`) and 3045-3052 (jig-host click)
- evidence: both handlers do `const anchor = slotfieldEl.querySelector([data-spatial-slot=i]); jigLit = index; if (anchor) openChooser(index, anchor);` — the slot nodes are only rebuilt by `renderSpatialSlots()` inside `renderCenter` (`shipworks.js:3713`), so they can be momentarily absent while `jigLit` is already set. `openChooser` itself is tolerant: `shipworks.js:4287` `chooserAnchor = anchorEl || slotfieldEl.querySelector(…)`, and its rAF focus loop retargets — the guard discards a call `openChooser` would have handled.
- suggested_fix: on a valid index call `openChooser(index, null)` unconditionally and keep the guard only to emit the `ui_deny` cue out of range.
- confidence: medium

### F-MENUS-04
- symptom: (legacy-only, no live player route) The local map's Close control and its own `M` key path go through `_close()` only via `ctx.screenManager.popScreen`, whereas the sibling starmap has a bus fallback (`ui:popScreen`) for bus-mounted hosts; a host that mounts screens by bus intent gets a silent dead close.
- severity: minor (conditional; not reachable on the default route — `src/ui/mapAuthority.js:6` and `src/ui/input.js:503` keep localmap for tools/checks, and `src/ui/uiRoot.js:1342-1358` converts `ui:pushScreen localmap` to galaxyMap)
- route: local map (legacy/tools) → Close button / `M` key
- owner: src/ui/screens/localmap.js:846-849 (`_close`)
- evidence: `localmap.js:846-849` `const sm = this._ctx && this._ctx.screenManager; if (sm && typeof sm.popScreen === 'function') sm.popScreen();` — no emit fallback; contrast `src/ui/screens/starmap.js:678-683` `closeScreen(ctx)` which falls back to `ctx.bus.emit('ui:popScreen', {})` after the same probe.
- suggested_fix: mirror starmap's `closeScreen` — try `popScreen`, else emit `ui:popScreen`.
- confidence: high (code), low (reachability)

